## Why This Is Asked
This question tests designing a real-time privacy-preserving federation with streaming updates, focusing on DP budgets, monotonic aggregation, replay protection, and fault tolerance.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time streaming aggregation with privacy guarantees
- Per-device DP budgeting and accounting
- Replay protection and clock skew handling
- Throughput considerations and backpressure in edge-to-cloud pipelines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate delta
function processDelta({device_id, ts, delta, nonce, dp_noise}) {
  if (nonce in usedNonces[device_id]) throw 'replay';
  usedNonces[device_id].add(nonce);
  if (ts <= lastTs[device_id]) delta = 0; // monotone
  // apply clipping
  delta = Math.max(-MAX_DELTA, Math.min(MAX_DELTA, delta));
  globalSum += delta + dp_noise;
  budgets[device_id] -= DP_COST;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test privacy budget exhaustion under burst traffic?
- How would you handle device churn and late arrivals without leaking budgets?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of user consent management, data retention policies, and privacy-preserving API design in a real-world context.

## Key Concepts
- Consent management and revocation handling
- Data retention and purging policies
- Privacy-preserving scoring architecture
- API versioning for backward compatibility
- Deterministic scoring for reproducibility

## Code Example
```javascript
async function computeCcaScore(input, consent, userIdHashed) {
  if (!consent) {
    return { cca_score: null, reason: 'consent_required' };
  }
  const score = Object.values(input).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) % 100;
  await persistence.saveScore(userIdHashed, { score, timestamp: Date.now() });
  return { cca_score: String(score) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model multi-tenant consent policies with different regulatory requirements (GDPR, CCPA)?
- How would you bucket revocation events for audit logging and compliance reporting?
- How would you handle consent synchronization across distributed services?
